 typing in the notes  from the meeting so you'll met with  Carrie Smith go to dues and put in all  this stuff you know underneath whatever  you need  and why I like this is I find it helpful  to refer back to you so I use this for  meetings when I'm having mean with  people on my team and we meet once a  month and I'll keep track of what we  said we were going to do and then I can  refer to it the next month when we meet  again to see what's been done and what  still needs to happen on top of that I  can add notes for all the different  types of documents that I want to share  so for example if I sign a new agreement  with Bank of America I would do a new  note I could call it agreement and then  I could go to my regular Explorer and  just drag in the PDF of the signed  agreement so you could drag in pictures  you could drag in agreements PDFs drag  in any files that you need to save and  it's all here and an easy-to-find format  so if I ever need to come back and find  out what was going on and dig deeper  into my notes I could have two choices  one I could click on my Bank of America  notebook and then search just man you  look down and say okay well this was  called my meeting notice of my agreement  and hopefully this will build as you do  a lot of work with your client so you  can manually sort through it here or you  can do a search and you can go at the  top here and you get search and you  search your notes and you could put in  whatever word you're looking for or  agreement or you know you're looking for  Harry Smith you put in Harry Smith and  I'll pull up only the notes that relate  to that client so that's how I would do  it and again I would repeat this for  every new client that I brought on that  I wanted the track you create in your  notebook it's all stored within the  clients stack and it's easy to keep up  to date and you have everything in one  central area and it's it's on your  computer it's on your phone it's on your  iPad any device that's connected to  Evernote you have instant access to all  the information you need and you can  easily edit it as well and when you do  it'll be edited across all your devices  to hopefully that helps a great question  for those of you watching like the video  please give it a thumbs up below and I'd  love to hear what you have to think if  you have a more specific question about  Evernote or another question for your  business leave it below I'd be happy to  do a video response thank you guys and  I'll see you soon
 

